<title>ITALY: Snia Fibre sees Q1 sales higher.</title>
<headline>Snia Fibre sees Q1 sales higher.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian chemicals and fibres group Snia Fibre, controlled by Fiat, showed sales in the first quarter of 1997 at 263 billion lire after 250 billion lire in the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>Operating profits were 11 billion lire after 10 billion lire previously, with a pretax profit of three billion lire after a pretax loss of one billion lire in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
